# tests/sub-run, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. `sub-run` is a worker verb — it exists so a job can dispatch
# work it will not wait for — and all three fixtures here were already workers.
# The client did two things neither of which was under test: it curried and ran
# them, which a worker does with prepare-request/run-request-then, and it polled
# the server for an object, which `caos get-hash` does.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --self:@=self.sh --delayed:@=delayed.sh --launch:@=launch.sh --settle:@=settle.sh
